# PHP & ExpressionEngine Conventions

- Use modern PHP (PHP 7.2+) syntax available in this project. Avoid deprecated features.
- Follow project namespaces under `ExpressionEngine\` where applicable. Core lives in [`system/ee/ExpressionEngine`](mdc:system/ee/ExpressionEngine).
- Prefer dependency injection over globals where the framework allows.
- Keep functions small with clear names; avoid deep nesting; return early on errors.
- Match existing code style and formatting in nearby files.
- Write high-verbosity, self-documenting code. Add concise comments only when non-obvious.
- Do not introduce TODO comments—implement or create an issue instead.

## File Locations

- Core classes, services, and models: [`system/ee/ExpressionEngine`](mdc:system/ee/ExpressionEngine)
- Legacy code resides under [`system/ee/legacy`](mdc:system/ee/legacy); avoid adding new code there.
- Addons integrate under `ExpressionEngine/Addon` structure when applicable.

## Security & Input Handling

- Escape output and validate input; use ExpressionEngine utilities for XSS and CSRF protection.
- Never trust user input; sanitize and validate before use.

## Testing

- For UI flows, add/adjust Cypress tests under [`tests/cypress`](mdc:tests/cypress).